  "format": "dsc60-business-writing-stage-v1",
  "status": "rewritten",
  "text": "Your weekly order list is ready for December 1\u20137, 2025. It suggests ordering **877 units across 112 product-and-store combinations**, with no purchase needed for the other 224. The list gives you suggested quantities for each store so you can review the orders without working out every quantity by hand.\n\nStart with the items flagged as likely to run out before the next delivery. There are **52 product-and-store combinations** flagged for review. Check these first before placing orders, and consider whether an earlier delivery is needed.\n\nThe weekly routine checks sales, stock in each store, deliveries on the way and your supplied buying rules. It works out quantities to cover the delivery wait plus the following week, allows for your stock buffer, subtracts stock and deliveries due in that period, and applies pack sizes and minimum order quantities. Review those pack-size purchases before ordering, as they can add substantially to the total.\n\nThe weekly calculation took **0.444 seconds** in the measured run. This repeatable calculation can be scheduled to prepare a fresh order list each week for you to review before placing orders.\n\nEstimated AI processing cost for this analysis: about US$0.56, using OpenAI\u2019s [published standard rates](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.1-sol).\n",
